Parent re-renders, so child re-renders. React re-renders child component whenever parent re-renders, regardless of prop changes—that's default behavior.

**Most common culprit:** Inline objects or functions passed as props.

```jsx
// Bad — new object ref each render
<Child data={{ name: 'John' }} />

// Bad — new function each render  
<Child onClick={() => handleClick()} />
```

Each render creates new object/function reference. Child sees "different" prop, re-renders.

**Fix:**

```jsx
// Move outside component
const DATA = { name: 'John' };
<Child data={DATA} />

// Or use useMemo
<Child data={useMemo(() => ({ name: 'John' }), [])} />
<Child onClick={useCallback(() => handleClick(), [])} />
```

**Verify it's actually unnecessary:** Add `React.memo` to child. If re-renders stop, props were changing. If they continue, parent re-rendering without prop change.

```jsx
const Child = React.memo(({ data }) => {
  console.log('Child rendered');
  return <div>{data.name}</div>;
});
```

Check console — if "Child rendered" logs every time even with memo, parent is re-rendering unnecessarily (look for state updates in parent).
